 "title": "October: the AI trade turned into a funding question, and the money rails stayed bullish",
 "summary": "October opened on **where AI agents spend money** (agentic commerce, crypto rails, card networks as the consensus loser) and closed on **who pays for the buildout**. With the 10-year near 5.2%, AI infra / neoclouds climbed to 23% of briefs by W43 on a credit scare (CoreWeave, hedge-fund degrossing), then cooled to 13% as enterprise demand gave the capex an underwriter. Crypto platforms were the month's steadiest narrative (13-21% every week, sentiment never broke), while the bank and telco clusters spiked and vanished within three weeks, mostly on one or two voices. Memory + optics is the open thread into November: written off in W40, emerging again by W44 (10%), then silent a week later.",
